the explosion left a crater around three  meters deep  flats in the surrounding residential  apartment blocks were destroyed  the blast shredded trees in the park  where children usually play  this was one of a number of attacks  across krematorsk in what was the  largest simultaneous barrage of rockets  on the city  since russia invaded ukraine more than  two months ago  we were sleeping and were awoken by a  series of explosions before there was  one massive blast thank god no one was  killed  a couple of kilometers away this parade  of shops and small businesses was also  hit  the city mayor says that 25 people were  injured in the attacks it's miraculous  that nobody was killed  soldiers have collected shrapnel to try  and identify the weapon that was used  i heard it was a rocket attack there was  a siren and then a huge explosion my  apartment is about 100 meters from here  and all the windows were blown out  the scale of the destruction here shows  you just how powerful the explosion  was there are tens of flats that have  been pretty much completely destroyed in  the blast  the ukrainian police say that they  believe that this was a russian air  strike and it comes in a time when the  ukrainian army say that russian forces  are trying to push in towards  kramertorsk and neighbouring cervansk  from the north  we drove north towards the  russian-controlled city of isiam  discarded blood-soaked bandages and a  stretcher  a wounded ukrainian soldier had been  transferred to an ambulance here only  minutes before  australia  cars are being shelled when our cars go  along the road they start shelling it  they shoot any vehicle ambulances  civilian vehicles it doesn't matter  ukrainian soldiers hide in the forest  from russian drones above  artillery shell casings litter the  ground  the soldiers won't let us film them but  they claim they have repelled three  waves of russian attacks in the last  week  they give us this video they claim shows  them retreating from russian artillery  fire  they say they are now holding their  defensive position  but what they currently can't do is stop  cities like kramatorsk from coming under  russian attacks  channel stratfor al jazeera krematorsk
 

